0.496,+0.616]. F1a=CONFIRMED F1b=CONFIRMED."], "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:low_measurement_reliability"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-085: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability", "score": 0.208, "reached_via": ["request matches RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY (0.28); FAM:SF-APPS-085 auto_has_risk RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY", "request matches METH:split_half_reliability (0.16); FAM:SF-APPS-085 auto_uses_method METH:split_half_reliability"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) is a stable player-season attribute.", "observed_result": "Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within). Attenuation: even a perfect predictor  [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Split-half r=0.215 / SB 0.355 is too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=102 connectors"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:low_measurement_reliability"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-086"}]}], "n_results": 4}

